# Albert FE — Project Overview & Architecture

> **Purpose:** This document describes the Albert frontend project at a high level, focusing on its architecture, runtime behavior, and key files. It is intended to be read by a refactoring engineer who needs to programmatically verify that the project continues to work after each change.

---

## 1. What This Project Is

Albert FE is a **React 18 monorepo of micro frontends (MFs)** built with Vite and the Vite-native **Module Federation** plugin (`@module-federation/vite`). The project serves a single browser application that consists of multiple independently deployable frontend units.

The project is managed with **npm workspaces** — there is a root `package.json` that defines workspaces `packages/*` and `apps/*`, and every subfolder is an independent Node package.

---

## 2. High-Level Architecture

The architecture is an **Application Shell (host)** that loads **micro frontends at runtime** via Module Federation.

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                         Browser                              │
│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │   host (shell)  — port 5000                          │   │
│  │   ┌──────────┐   ┌────────────────────────────────┐  │   │
│  │   │ Sidebar  │   │ <main>                         │  │   │
│  │   │ (host)   │   │ ┌──────────────────────────┐  │  │   │
│  │   │          │   │ │ mf-causes — port 5001      │  │  │   │
│  │   │          │   │ │ (loaded at runtime via MF) │  │  │   │
│  │   └──────────┘   │ └──────────────────────────┘  │  │   │
│  │                  └────────────────────────────────┘  │   │
│  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │
│                                                              │
│  Shared packages consumed at build time (npm workspaces)     │
│  @albert-fe/ui-kit  @albert-fe/logs  @albert-fe/api-client │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Key Principles

- **Host = shell only**: The host app contains routing (`react-router-dom`), a sidebar, auth context, permissions context, and the layout container. All business logic lives inside MFs.
- **MFs are independently buildable**: Each micro frontend has its own `vite.config.js`, `package.json`, and build output in `dist/`.
- **Shared dependencies are deduplicated**: `react` and `react-dom` are declared `singleton: true` in the Module Federation `shared` config so only one instance exists across the runtime.

