## 3. Apps & Their Roles

### 3.1 Host (`apps/host/`)

- **Port in dev**: 5000
- **Role**: Application shell. Handles:
  - `react-router-dom` routing (`BrowserRouter`)
  - Authentication via Keycloak (`AuthContext`)
  - Permission-based sidebar navigation (`PermissionsContext`)
  - Dynamic loading of remote micro frontends via Module Federation
- **Has test setup**: yes (`vitest.config.js`, `src/test/setup.js`)
- **Builds to**: `apps/host/dist/`
- **Entry**: `index.html` → `src/main.jsx`

### 3.2 MF Causes (`apps/mf-causes/`)

- **Port in dev**: 5001
- **Role**: A micro frontend that manages "Cases" (a business-domain feature). It exposes two components via Module Federation:
  - `./Component` → `src/Component.jsx` (the main page content rendered in the `<main>` area)
  - `./SidebarPanel` → `src/SidebarPanel.jsx` (the sidebar panel rendered inside the host sidebar)
- **Has test setup**: yes (`vitest.config.js`, `src/test/setup.js`)
- **Builds to**: `apps/mf-causes/dist/`
- **Entry**: `index.html` → `src/main.jsx` (standalone mode only)
- **Special note**: Has a `casesStore.js` using `useSyncExternalStore` for shared state, and `cases/useCases.js` hook.

### 3.3 Exemple Components (`apps/exemple-components/`)

- **Port in dev**: 5002
- **Role**: A **showcase/playground app** for the UI Kit. It is **not** a micro frontend and is consumed by nobody. It just renders all `ui-kit` components on one page so developers can see and interact with them.
- **Has test setup**: no
- **Builds to**: not relevant (dev-only)
- **Entry**: `index.html` → `src/main.jsx`

