## 4. Shared Packages (`packages/`)

These are consumed internally via npm workspaces (`@albert-fe/*`). They are **not** published to npm; the workspace symlinks make them available.

### 4.1 `@albert-fe/ui-kit`

- **Role**: Shared **design system** (React components + CSS tokens).
- **Has tests**: yes (vitest + jsdom + testing-library)
- **Build**: the `build` script is a no-op — it prints a message and exits. The package is **consumed as source** by all apps. This is intentional.
- **Entry**: `src/index.js` (barrel file that re-exports all components)
- **CSS**: `src/styles/base.css` defines CSS custom properties (design tokens) and is imported at the top of `src/index.js`, meaning consuming apps get the tokens automatically when they import any component.

### 4.2 `@albert-fe/logs`

- **Role**: Minimal logging utility. Exports `createLogger(scope)` and a default `logger`.
- **Has tests**: yes (vitest, node environment)
- **Build**: none needed (pure JS module)
- **Entry**: `src/index.js`
- **Note**: `createLogger` wraps `console` methods with a `[albert-fe][scope] timestamp — message` prefix.

### 4.3 `@albert-fe/api-client`

- **Role**: Shared HTTP client + Keycloak auth + API services.
- **Has tests**: yes (vitest, node environment)
- **Build**: none needed (pure JS module)
- **Entry**: `src/index.js` (barrel file)
- **Key modules**:
  - `HttpClient.js`: generic HTTP class using native `fetch`
  - `ApiService.js`: thin wrapper over `HttpClient` with an auth interceptor
  - `auth/keycloakService.js`: Keycloak initialization, token management, auto-refresh
  - `auth/sessionStorage.js`: sessionStorage helpers for tokens
  - `interceptors/authInterceptor.js`: injects Bearer tokens into requests
  - `services/cases/CasesService.js`: API calls for cases
  - `services/permissions/PermissionsService.js`: API calls for permissions
  - `errors/ApiError.js`: custom error class

