## 8. Environment Variables

All env files live at the **project root**. Variables prefixed with `VITE_` are exposed to the frontend. Key variables:

| Variable                     | Purpose                                  |
| ---------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| `VITE_MF_CAUSES_URL`         | URL to the mf-causes `remoteEntry.js`    |
| `VITE_MF_REGULATORY_URL`     | URL to the mfRegulatory `remoteEntry.js` |
| `VITE_API_URL`               | Backend-for-Frontend base URL            |
| `VITE_KEYCLOAK_URL`          | Keycloak server URL                      |
| `VITE_KEYCLOAK_REALM`        | Keycloak realm                           |
| `VITE_KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID`    | Keycloak client ID                       |
| `BFF_TARGET`                 | Vite proxy target in dev mode            |
| `VITE_PREVIEW_ALLOWED_HOSTS` | Allows external hosts in preview mode    |

Files (in precedence order):

1. `.env` (defaults, committed)
2. `.env.development` / `.env.staging` / `.env.production` (committed)
3. `.env.local` / `.env.[mode].local` (gitignored, dev overrides)

